# Scheduly Frontend Data And Auth

- Use `src/lib/api-client.ts` for backend calls; never create ad hoc Axios clients or hardcode `localhost`.
- Read the backend base URL through `VITE_API_URL` via `src/config/env.ts` (default `http://localhost:4001`).
- Keep session, CSRF, and storage access centralized (`auth-store` / `cookies`); do not log or render tokens.
- Cookie name: `scheduly.csrf`. Header: `x-csrf-token`.
- Let `api-client` send cookies (`withCredentials`), attach CSRF on unsafe methods, and clear the session on `401` (except login/`/me` probes).
- Logout must hit `POST /api/auth/logout` before clearing local session.
- Envelope: `{ data: T }`. Lists are full arrays (no pagination). DELETE returns 204.
- Put API functions in `features/<domain>/api` and TanStack Query hooks in `features/<domain>/hooks`.
- Query keys live in `src/lib/query-keys.ts` (`currentUser`, `students`, `subjects`, `classes`). Invalidate affected keys after every mutation.
- Payment toggles use `PATCH /api/classes/:classId/payment-status`. Do not PATCH `paymentStatus` as a generic class update.
- Use `getErrorMessage` for backend errors, especially `401`, `403`, `404`, and `409`.
- Zod-parse payloads at the API boundary (`src/types/schemas.ts`).
